    "comment": {
      "comments": [
        {
          "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/issue/12501473/comment/13009150",
          "id": "13009150",
          "author": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=stillalex",
            "name": "stillalex",
            "key": "alex.parvulescu",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?ownerId=alex.parvulescu&avatarId=41133",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&ownerId=alex.parvulescu&avatarId=41133",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&ownerId=alex.parvulescu&avatarId=41133",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&ownerId=alex.parvulescu&avatarId=41133"
            },
            "displayName": "Alex Deparvu",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "America/Los_Angeles"
          },
          "body": "Attaching patch for lucene Field creation. I replaced all the Field constructors with the proper ones to skip the intern() call.\n\nThe same issue seems to apply to org.apache.lucene.index.Term, it is also heavily used, and now provides a constructor that allows skipping the intern() call.\n\nDo you think that should be addressed in this issue too?",
          "updateAuthor": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=stillalex",
            "name": "stillalex",
            "key": "alex.parvulescu",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?ownerId=alex.parvulescu&avatarId=41133",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&ownerId=alex.parvulescu&avatarId=41133",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&ownerId=alex.parvulescu&avatarId=41133",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&ownerId=alex.parvulescu&avatarId=41133"
            },
            "displayName": "Alex Deparvu",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "America/Los_Angeles"
          },
          "created": "2011-03-21T14:51:13.774+0000",
          "updated": "2011-03-21T14:51:13.774+0000"
        },
        {
          "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/issue/12501473/comment/13009611",
          "id": "13009611",
          "author": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=mreutegg",
            "name": "mreutegg",
            "key": "mreutegg",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?ownerId=mreutegg&avatarId=18658",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&ownerId=mreutegg&avatarId=18658",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&ownerId=mreutegg&avatarId=18658",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&ownerId=mreutegg&avatarId=18658"
            },
            "displayName": "Marcel Reutegger",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "Europe/Zurich"
          },
          "body": "Generally the patch look OK.\n\nI've identified two issues:\n- IndexMigrationTest (line 71) and NodeIndexer (line 745): the field names still need to be interned. The names are not one of the already interned constants.\n\nRegarding Term usage: I think we should create a separate issue for that.",
          "updateAuthor": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=mreutegg",
            "name": "mreutegg",
            "key": "mreutegg",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?ownerId=mreutegg&avatarId=18658",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&ownerId=mreutegg&avatarId=18658",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&ownerId=mreutegg&avatarId=18658",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&ownerId=mreutegg&avatarId=18658"
